  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The analysis relies on province-level sub-regional data from a single coastal province, which may limit the applicability of the interaction dynamic to inland or less economically active regions.",
      "what": "Using a Super-SBM model, exploratory spatial data analysis, and a panel VAR model, the study analyzed the interaction between land space utilization efficiency and high-quality development across Fujian province from 2005 to 2023. Higher utilization efficiency concentrated in Xiamen, Nanping, and Longyan, while highly coupled regions were limited to coastal hubs like Xiamen, Fuzhou, and Quanzhou. Econometric modeling revealed that the positive impact of high-quality development on land resource allocation is significantly stronger than the reverse influence of land efficiency on high-quality development.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that improving land utilization efficiency alone is insufficient to drive high-quality regional growth, reversing the common assumption that land optimization acts as a primary catalyst for broader socioeconomic development."
    }
  },
